{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-112400",
  "enisaUuid": "f3107af1-c6f0-3d29-b124-6cbaee74f6c2",
  "description": "When the `allowed_scopes` configuration is enabled, the OAuth2 token introspection mechanism does not immediately invalidate a token in the cache after a revocation request. This results in a scenario where an access token that was introspected immediately before a revocation request may be returned again to the client after revocation, until the relevant cache entry is cleared.\n\nThe security consequence is that a revoked access token may be re-issued to the client during the cache lifetime. While the re-issued token is not treated as valid for API authorization, affected users may be unable to obtain a new valid access token until the cache is cleared, which can disrupt authentication flows.",
  "datePublished": "Oct 28, 2026, 7:21:34 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Oct 28, 2026, 7:21:34 PM",
  "baseScore": 3.1,
  "baseScoreVersion": "3.1",
  "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L",
